180:  l_0=2(N+a-2),\qquad l_1=2(1-b),\qquad
181:  l_2=2(N-2).                                        \tag{DZ.11}
182: \]
183: The based ratio of each diagonal entry is its displayed angular
184: factor times the exponential of its actual based periodic
185: logarithm. This follows by subtracting its winding from the full
186: nonzero loop, on the same \(q\)-disc.
187: 
188: For every integer \(d\) use the actual based quaternion contraction
189: \[
190:  H_d(s,\theta)=
191:   (\sin\vartheta(s)e^{id\theta}+j\cos\vartheta(s))
192:   (\sin\vartheta(s)+j\cos\vartheta(s))^{-1},          \tag{DZ.12}
193: \]
194: where \(\vartheta\) is smooth, constant at \(0,\pi/2\) near the two
195: ends. Thus \(H_d(0,\theta)=1\), \(H_d(1,\theta)=e^{id\theta}\), and
196: both parameter endpoints are one. For
197: \(Q=n_0+j\overline{n_1}\), set
198: \[
199:               T_i(Q)=H_t Q H_{l_i-t}.               \tag{DZ.13}
200: \]
201: At its second radial end this has the two complex factors
202: \((e^{il_i\theta},e^{i(2t-l_i)\theta})\), exactly the angular part
203: of \(D_{i,*}^{-1}D_i\). Multiply by the diagonal exponentials of
204: the retained periodic unit logarithms, with a radial cutoff zero
205: at the first end and one at the second. The resulting
206: \(\mathcal K_i\) is based and periodic and satisfies
207: \[
208:  \mathcal K_i(0,\theta)=1,\quad
209:  \mathcal K_i(1,\theta)=D_{i,*}^{-1}D_i,\quad
210:                    zD_{i,*}\mathcal K_i(1,\theta)=zD_i. \tag{DZ.14}
211: \]
212: On the tube of the \(i\)-th curve use
213: \((z,n)\mapsto(z,\mathcal K_i(s(|z|),\theta)n)\).
214: The last equality is its exact second-vertex collar equality;
215: near the first vertex it is the identity. The three curve interiors
216: are disjoint, so the three maps glue to the two vertex maps.
217: 
218: For the original, nonlinear germs retain the full normal rescaling
219: \(R_\tau(z,n)=(z,\tau n)\). The conjugation
220: \(R_\tau^{-1}FR_\tau\) extends smoothly to \(\tau=0\) with the
